<span id="workspaces-title" class="anchor-alias" aria-hidden="true"></span><span
  id="workspaces-close-title"
  class="anchor-alias"
  aria-hidden="true"></span>
<section
  class="feature-copy-grid feature-copy-grid--top"
  aria-labelledby="workspaces-section-0"
>
  <div>
    <h2
      id="workspaces-section-0"
    >
      Name it once. Keep it up to date as you browse.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Save this window or start a new set</h3><p>
        Open the space control in the command panel or type /space.
        Anyone can save the current window or create a blank space.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Bring your Spaces from Arc</h3><p>
        In Bring Your Tabs (type /bring-tabs), choose Arc, and each Space you
        pick becomes a space here, with its pinned tabs, its Today tabs and
        its folders as tab groups.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Return without rebuilding the set</h3><p>
        A bound space automatically saves its tabs and groups as you browse
        and returns after relaunch. Switching replaces the current window’s set;
        a space already open elsewhere brings that window forward.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Tell spaces apart at a glance</h3><p>
        Give each space a colour and a symbol. The current space shows at the
        start of the Island; click it to switch, edit, reorder or delete a
        space, with Undo.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>You decide what belongs together</h3><p>
        Create groups and assign tabs yourself. Blanc saves those choices; it
        does not detect tasks or organize tabs by meaning.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="workspaces-section-1">
  <div>
    <h2 id="workspaces-section-1">
      Support Blanc and keep your saved spaces.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Available on every desktop platform</h3><p>
        Blanc Spaces is free for everyone on macOS, Windows and Linux. Blanc
        Patron is an optional subscription that supports Blanc’s
        development; it doesn’t unlock any feature.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Existing spaces remain yours</h3><p>
        Your spaces stay on this device, in this profile, and keep updating
        as you browse. Nothing about them depends on a subscription.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Keep private browsing separate</h3><p>
        Private tabs are excluded from saved spaces. When a switch would
        discard private tabs or an unsaved window, Blanc asks you to make an
        explicit choice.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<aside class="truth-note" aria-labelledby="workspaces-note-title">
  <h2 id="workspaces-note-title">
    Saved on this device, within this profile.
  </h2>
  <p>
    Blanc Spaces are device-local and profile-scoped. They do not sync
    across devices or move tabs between local profiles. Saving a space
    preserves its tab setup, not every page’s running state.
  </p>
</aside>
